        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your 89-year-old female patient, admitted on 08/10/2016 due to an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, clinical examination revealed decreased breath sounds, prolonged expiration, and significant dyspnoea. Oxygen saturation was reduced at rest. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemic respiratory failure. Chest X-ray showed pulmonary hyperinflation consistent with COPD. Blood tests demonstrated mild inflammatory markers. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and supportive intravenous fluids. She responded well to treatment with progressive clinical improvement. Prior to discharge, patient education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation recognition was provided. We recommend close follow-up in your practice and optimisation of her maintenance inhaler regimen. Please do not hesitate to contact us should you require further information.</div>"
            },
